#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688376 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71f0f728-375a-56bb-9e0d-d6827df2767a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688368} {:answer/id #uuid "8b1657ce-0efc-5822-8d02-3aeb92d7403e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688371} {:answer/id #uuid "a09ae09d-164b-5d81-a60c-62a022c39a03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688373} {:answer/id #uuid "c77ef708-bfec-5967-9779-b50ed9fc1b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688374} {:answer/id #uuid "e5e425d0-79a7-5c25-8ff1-23bf40975d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c77ef708-bfec-5967-9779-b50ed9fc1b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688374} :answer-field/id #uuid "530da1d6-029a-52b0-98ff-88515deb48a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e19be8df-0162-5666-8be4-94e618981df2" :question/problem "Find $t$, if $2\\mathbf{a}_1-t\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{b}$ and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\quad \\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Isolate the term containing $t$ using vector subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-t\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ t\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} &=2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ t\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first component is $0t=0$, which places no restriction on $t$. The second component requires\n\n$$\n-2t=-3\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad t=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nCheck this candidate in the whole vector:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\ne \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe third component instead requires $4t=5$, or $t=\\frac{5}{4}$. The two nonzero components require different scalars; the true equation $0=0$ in the first component cannot resolve that conflict. Select **No solution**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688611 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08325cf0-ff6e-5134-855a-bb328981c2fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688605} {:answer/id #uuid "61ac8907-9fff-5dfd-916b-1fb199b40db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688606} {:answer/id #uuid "673d5c5d-2316-52ae-87dd-a03672aa0cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688607} {:answer/id #uuid "8eded1ff-a780-5b1f-a503-ad3d4234a38a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688608} {:answer/id #uuid "ad14cada-a76b-50fa-83d9-465cae14e2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8eded1ff-a780-5b1f-a503-ad3d4234a38a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688608} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae3ec992-5cc1-54f2-8662-5d0eb9ae4dd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688610}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f39074b5-f6ac-5ded-906e-d4f431ec43d9" :question/problem "Find $l$, if $2{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2}=0$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $l$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 2\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+l\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $l=6.$ This value satisfies every component."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ff6f72-fa9c-5dd9-a628-000cffe8b4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688613} {:answer/id #uuid "18e5126a-bc33-556e-9166-a698aa0b4a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688615} {:answer/id #uuid "1ef4d9ed-897f-5a04-b40c-27287698ea94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688617} {:answer/id #uuid "7ca65cd5-cfdf-5453-a7bf-348a4200644c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688629} {:answer/id #uuid "b7154bdb-d78c-5765-b948-bab6ba57d679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7154bdb-d78c-5765-b948-bab6ba57d679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688634} :answer-field/id #uuid "16b98c54-3efd-58cc-943a-d2eb0c8ace9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "65dde477-f720-5c35-9f19-b5ae5761d0cc" :question/problem "Find $l$, if $2{a}_{1}-l{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $l$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-l{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-l\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =2\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $l=3.$ This value satisfies every component."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c005d91-7a36-5a6e-9dab-ef8922d27edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688616} {:answer/id #uuid "3293d376-1c53-544a-8fb7-7be2ef9cb8ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688618} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed2b620-bf24-5975-ab3a-ce5c93071f28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688619} {:answer/id #uuid "59313a23-2acb-51fd-b5f6-6f85043553f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688622} {:answer/id #uuid "f526d944-dfe5-5d34-8fae-693f0d708709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f526d944-dfe5-5d34-8fae-693f0d708709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688639} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba313ab3-c5e4-55d0-9db9-fc91177e7865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "68578f58-7e63-5891-84dc-5e42b32a4f28" :question/problem "Find $q$, if $2{a}_{1}-q{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $q$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-q{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-q\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =2\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $q=-6.$ This value satisfies every component."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688632 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7137caec-1801-5530-be35-bc1407e8e07d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688626} {:answer/id #uuid "84cf36ad-f153-5d41-b30b-ed60b44d8571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688630} {:answer/id #uuid "bb07acdf-0ae4-5f93-900e-c6fc967bbffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688636} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd327e1-a604-5237-8dbc-f73f26b29c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688637} {:answer/id #uuid "ffad8570-4c77-5f76-831f-d36bb850a8a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84cf36ad-f153-5d41-b30b-ed60b44d8571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688630} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfe10e14-4906-5ea0-ad32-718c7d6ef02c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9c711d86-4e7d-5183-9e3c-c1f0443d246b" :question/problem "Find $q$, if $3{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $q$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+q\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $q=2.$ This value satisfies every component."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688633 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53b1e405-08b7-5557-a50d-8b9d0b960418" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688620} {:answer/id #uuid "53eb35c4-7002-573e-b13f-80ad0744addb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688621} {:answer/id #uuid "672f67a6-e358-54a8-af73-bc23c7e45728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688624} {:answer/id #uuid "7b0cd383-4828-5c5a-af30-467df545610a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688628} {:answer/id #uuid "868af1e4-3189-59bc-bd04-a05b2e3918c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53b1e405-08b7-5557-a50d-8b9d0b960418" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688620} :answer-field/id #uuid "79bdda08-950f-5878-9d07-9ca48190bbc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b3f9ffbb-5a91-5049-98f3-600ca3880a6f" :question/problem "Find $k$, if $2{a}_{1}-k{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-k{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-k\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =2\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $k=0.$ This value satisfies every component."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705668 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "084d642d-2000-5031-b878-1c31a3369acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705660} {:answer/id #uuid "0adb3a1b-414f-5134-bca4-9b603bd1c5cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705661} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca5f5a4-807b-58cc-a121-e8ced7b18886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705663} {:answer/id #uuid "60a0ca5a-e273-5b27-8a89-49c5eb39be32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705666} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a1e307-5096-5555-95d2-2ec5fbcf0932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8a1e307-5096-5555-95d2-2ec5fbcf0932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705677} :answer-field/id #uuid "59bc56ab-57e0-58c5-b5b9-22504b9074b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a5c2fae2-7ea9-5a2c-9c93-e5315eb7f23a" :question/problem "The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be $\\mathbf{a}_2$ if\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A pair containing a nonzero vector $\\mathbf{a}_1$ is linearly dependent exactly when the other vector is a scalar multiple of $\\mathbf{a}_1$. The scalar is allowed to be zero.\n\nHere the correct choice is\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}=0\\mathbf{a}_1.\n$$\nFor the other choices, a first coordinate of $1$ is impossible because every multiple of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ starts with $0$. Among the remaining nonzero choices, the second and third coordinate multipliers disagree: they are $2$ and $3$, $-1$ and $1$, or $\\frac{3}{2}$ and $\\frac{2}{3}$. None is a scalar multiple.\n\nUsing the definition directly,\n$$\n0\\mathbf{a}_1+1\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\nThe coefficients $(x_1,x_2)=(0,1)$ are not both zero, so the set is linearly dependent. A nontrivial dependence requires the coefficients to be not both zero; it does not require both coefficients to be nonzero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705674 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f84da31-5996-5e4f-a3ee-7ce12001f1ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705665} {:answer/id #uuid "ab981ba9-f210-5a14-b902-ffebd2958db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705670} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c0c426-07ed-536b-8836-88e0dc9d9712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705671} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b3f7da-fcf6-506e-a975-8e04f021b6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705673} {:answer/id #uuid "dfba1552-06f9-5ea4-bfc7-4a269a2b4af5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0c0c426-07ed-536b-8836-88e0dc9d9712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705671} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd1b30f9-6a3a-5d7c-90b3-d1000d673e62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d82f6dbd-1a69-54f4-b28a-78061fb3c06c" :question/problem "The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be $\\mathbf{a}_2$ if\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Because $\\mathbf{a}_1$ is nonzero, the pair is linearly dependent exactly when $\\mathbf{a}_2=c\\mathbf{a}_1$ for one scalar $c$ that works in every coordinate.\n\nThe vector\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}=3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}=3\\mathbf{a}_1\n$$\nuses the same multiplier, $3$, in both coordinates. The other choices either change only one sign, interchange the coordinates, or use different multipliers.\n\nTo connect this to the definition, rearrange the equality:\n$$\n3\\mathbf{a}_1-\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\nThus $x_1=3$ and $x_2=-1$ solve $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{0}$. Since these coefficients are not both zero, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e7d67d-053b-54db-aed0-6b9a87cc8c20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705659} {:answer/id #uuid "0bebbf84-63a9-5902-9383-629248ac452f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705662} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6c9c64-4587-5af4-b109-27669344b9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705667} {:answer/id #uuid "a83dbbb1-579d-5c8e-95de-82a7366e6d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705669} {:answer/id #uuid "c44f4ed2-e6de-516d-85ac-e721e568091a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b6c9c64-4587-5af4-b109-27669344b9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705667} :answer-field/id #uuid "04fa36b5-c3a6-5feb-9059-23ff59ef3041" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f67662b4-6906-5907-9cdc-de46b6d3d6f0" :question/problem "The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be $\\mathbf{a}_2$ if\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Because $\\mathbf{a}_1$ is nonzero, we need one scalar $c$ such that $\\mathbf{a}_2=c\\mathbf{a}_1$ in all three coordinates. A multiple of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ must have second coordinate $0$.\n\nThe vector\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_2=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}_1\n$$\nsatisfies every coordinate. In particular, multiplying $-4$ by $-\\frac{1}{2}$ gives $2$. The choice with middle coordinate $1$ fails even though its first and last coordinates fit; the other choices use inconsistent multipliers in the nonzero coordinates.\n\nRearranging gives\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}_1+\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\nSo $x_1=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $x_2=1$ give a solution whose coefficients are not both zero. This proves linear dependence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20844911-f1dc-56ad-922a-208a14d6066a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705825} {:answer/id #uuid "8538dfdc-f160-599e-a5d9-58fe63a6e3f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705839} {:answer/id #uuid "ad13460b-3c28-52ad-bad9-21121f2efd95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705842} {:answer/id #uuid "bec1e64c-0ada-5acb-a9fc-aa1d7f963204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705846} {:answer/id #uuid "e0cff523-d3ed-5463-a055-9a8016b6a7b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bec1e64c-0ada-5acb-a9fc-aa1d7f963204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705846} :answer-field/id #uuid "c15a75c9-1103-5a89-bd9d-8ebe29e9b9ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b6486b02-9fbd-5750-809b-8d4c1bc07b11" :question/problem "The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be $\\mathbf{a}_2$ if\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Because $\\mathbf{a}_1$ is nonzero, we need **one common scalar** $c$ such that $\\mathbf{a}_2=c\\mathbf{a}_1$ in every coordinate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{a}_2 &=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)(-12) \\\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)(-6) \\\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)(-6)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\mathbf{a}_1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe other choices fail a coordinate check:\n\n- The candidate $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ requires multipliers $-\\frac{1}{6}$ and $\\frac{1}{6}$ in coordinates $1$ and $2$, respectively. They disagree.\n- The candidate $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ requires multipliers $-\\frac{1}{6}$ and $\\frac{1}{3}$ in coordinates $1$ and $2$, respectively. They disagree.\n- The candidate $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ requires multipliers $\\frac{1}{6}$ and $\\frac{1}{3}$ in coordinates $1$ and $2$, respectively. They disagree.\n- The candidate $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ requires multipliers $\\frac{1}{6}$ and $\\frac{1}{3}$ in coordinates $1$ and $2$, respectively. They disagree.\n\nRearrange the scalar-multiple equality:\n$$\n\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\mathbf{a}_1-\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\nThus $(x_1,x_2)=(\\frac{1}{3},-1)$ solves $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{0}$. These coefficients are **not both zero**, so the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22c6349a-003f-5bc9-b82d-aeccc2303824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705826} {:answer/id #uuid "4c1bc4f6-277e-5cb8-8239-944f9bcf9ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705830} {:answer/id #uuid "63aa5aae-931a-5018-91dc-accd70f3123c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705832} {:answer/id #uuid "6c3b4b1c-b1ee-54d0-adf2-1040c678c8ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705834} {:answer/id #uuid "6ebee206-cbc8-5917-a749-fc15d1b2c17c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63aa5aae-931a-5018-91dc-accd70f3123c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705832} :answer-field/id #uuid "e222c5e1-fae1-5df5-bb28-076892716f40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ba91be3b-bde0-5aed-b962-90d0afe37a87" :question/problem "The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be $\\mathbf{a}_2$ if\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_1=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Because $\\mathbf{a}_1$ is nonzero, we need **one common scalar** $c$ such that $\\mathbf{a}_2=c\\mathbf{a}_1$ in every coordinate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{a}_2 &=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\begin{bmatrix}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)(-4) \\\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)(-4) \\\\ \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)(-4)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &= \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\mathbf{a}_1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe other choices fail a coordinate check:\n\n- The candidate $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ requires multipliers $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\frac{1}{4}$ in coordinates $1$ and $2$, respectively. They disagree.\n- The candidate $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ requires multipliers $1$ and $\\frac{1}{2}$ in coordinates $1$ and $2$, respectively. They disagree.\n- The candidate $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ requires multipliers $-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\frac{1}{2}$ in coordinates $1$ and $2$, respectively. They disagree.\n- The candidate $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ requires multipliers $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $1$ in coordinates $1$ and $3$, respectively. They disagree.\n\nRearrange the scalar-multiple equality:\n$$\n\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\mathbf{a}_1-\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\nThus $(x_1,x_2)=(\\frac{1}{2},-1)$ solves $x_1\\mathbf{a}_1+x_2\\mathbf{a}_2=\\mathbf{0}$. These coefficients are **not both zero**, so the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186705850 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141f16b9-1d8a-5e95-a5df-d1b4d1d8ff85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705824} {:answer/id #uuid "321f6d2d-550e-5560-b005-387eee73b5be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705827} {:answer/id #uuid "47354db4-8847-5604-a903-8092c0a90085" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186705829} {:answer/id #uuid "d4c119f9-be0e-5650-9151-373444f6062c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref